    "title": "Cooper Flagg Misses Insane Alley-Oop Slam That Could've Been An Insane Start To His NBA Career [VIDEO] - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shabiha Akter ,\n19 minutes ago\nhttps://www.totalprosports.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Flagg-1-800x450.jpg Cooper Flagg’s failed dunk (Image Credits: X/@Sportsline) Cooper Flagg has officially begun his debut season with the Dallas Mavericks. The No.1 overall pick acknowledged that adapting to NBA terminology took some effort . But he remains fully determined to master it.\nOn Wednesday, Flagg made his much-anticipated debut as the Mavericks faced the San Antonio Spurs. The moment marked history, as he became the first player from Maine ever to play in an NBA game when the ball was tipped.\nSoon after the game tipped off, Flagg nearly created a highlight moment to start his NBA career. He ran through the defense and soared toward the rim for an alley-oop attempt. It could have been a spectacular start, but the ball rimmed out.\nFlagg’s debut night did not go as he might have envisioned. He was held scoreless in the first half. He recorded six rebounds and zero assists, as the Mavericks trailed the Spurs 60–51 at halftime.\nTim MacMahon Weighs In On Copper Flagg’s Role On The Court Cooper Flagg (Image Credits: Imagn) Before the Mavericks’ season opener, NBA insider Tim MacMahon shared details about how Dallas plans to utilize Flagg on the court.\n“ He’s going to have the ball in his hands. They want him, and believe that he will impact the game in a lot of different ways: scoring, facilitating, rebounding, and especially as a disruptive, dominant type of defensive player. There are no kid gloves with Cooper Flagg, ” MacMahon said.\nWith Flagg taking a key role on the floor, the Mavericks are expected to make a strong playoff run in the Western Conference this season. The organization has expressed full confidence in Flagg. Now, the responsibility falls squarely on Flagg’s shoulders to live up to the expectations surrounding his NBA journey.\nThe post originally published on .",
